WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:07.036
A quick tour of the desktop app, in sidebar order, with every button named exactly as it appears on screen.

2
00:00:08.736 --> 00:00:10.540
Overview summarises the app.

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:18.528
Mission Control shows live mainnet telemetry: the latest validated ledger, network health, fee pressure and the gate status.

4
00:00:18.978 --> 00:00:21.376
Open it before relying on any reading.

5
00:00:21.376 --> 00:00:26.552
If the ledger number is climbing every few seconds, you are connected and current.

6
00:00:26.552 --> 00:00:29.645
If it stops, readings are stale until it resumes.

7
00:00:31.345 --> 00:00:32.932
Verification is the gate.

8
00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:39.661
Enter the account, and optionally a destination and amount, run it, and read the verdict, then each check.

9
00:00:39.661 --> 00:00:41.883
Copy the receipt into your records.

10
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:45.262
Provenance traces where a counterparty came from.

11
00:00:45.262 --> 00:00:51.357
Paste the address and press Trace provenance to see its real age and the account that first funded it.

12
00:00:51.807 --> 00:00:56.738
Credentials lists the on-ledger credentials an account holds and who issued them.

13
00:00:56.738 --> 00:01:01.791
Domain Grid shows permissioned domains, their rules, and which amendments are live.

14
00:01:03.491 --> 00:01:06.900
Exposure Analysis puts a position's risks in one view.

15
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.129
Set your jurisdiction first, so the Travel Rule threshold is right.

16
00:01:11.579 --> 00:01:14.314
Portfolio and Radar watches several wallets.

17
00:01:14.314 --> 00:01:19.536
Enter an address and a label, press Add to book, and the radar keeps re-checking it.

18
00:01:19.986 --> 00:01:22.866
Order Book takes a currency code and an issuer.

19
00:01:22.866 --> 00:01:29.117
Press Read this book to see listed and funded depth, the unfunded share, the spread and the mid price.

20
00:01:29.567 --> 00:01:36.777
Pool Governance shows who votes an A M M pool's fee, on what share of its L P tokens, and who holds the auction slot.

21
00:01:38.477 --> 00:01:41.326
Control Surface answers who can move a treasury.

22
00:01:41.326 --> 00:01:48.269
Press Read control surface to see the master key, the signer list, the minimum signers and what is locked in reserve.

23
00:01:48.719 --> 00:01:51.482
Issuance shows a token from the issuer's side.

24
00:01:51.482 --> 00:01:57.189
If too few holder lines could be read, it withholds the concentration figure rather than guess.

25
00:01:57.639 --> 00:01:59.964
Authority runs the six issuer checks.

26
00:01:59.964 --> 00:02:04.551
Press Certify authority for the verdict, the ledger index and the digest.

27
00:02:05.001 --> 00:02:09.208
Passport packages an asset's posture into a signed record.

28
00:02:09.208 --> 00:02:14.067
Press Generate passport, then copy it as JSON or CSV, or export it.

29
00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:19.853
Audit Trail is a wallet's history with compliance details attached.

30
00:02:19.853 --> 00:02:23.085
Settlement shows what a transaction really delivered.

31
00:02:23.535 --> 00:02:26.991
Ledger and Policy holds your adjudication history.

32
00:02:26.991 --> 00:02:38.468
Step through it with previous and next, draft and simulate policy changes, open investigations, and press Export for a file with a SHA-256 chain-of-custody signature.

33
00:02:40.168 --> 00:02:42.825
Check an Address is free, ten times a month.

34
00:02:42.825 --> 00:02:47.293
Remember that nothing recorded against an address is not the same as safe.

35
00:02:47.743 --> 00:02:50.646
Inbox reads tokens strangers have sent you.

36
00:02:50.646 --> 00:02:57.599
A familiar ticker from an issuer with no obligations is an impersonation, and is flagged as uncashable.

37
00:02:58.049 --> 00:03:02.636
Token Rights reads what an N F T's issuer can still do after you own it.

38
00:03:03.086 --> 00:03:08.633
Ledger Sync compares what four public servers report right now, free and without an account.

39
00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:17.788
And the Agent and the Ledger Garden let you explore: walk from issuer to asset to holder to evidence, and ask the agent about what you find.

40
00:03:17.788 --> 00:03:21.456
The full reference for every screen is in lesson seventeen.
